Title: FINAL LAP
Author: Tyler Brooks
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. UNIVERSITY CAMPUS - ESTABLISHING - DAY

Autumn. Banners for the Senior Invitational flutter over the aquatics center.

INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - MORNING

NINA VASQUEZ attacks intervals. COACH ALMA REYES watches, arms crossed.
ALMA
You're racing the clock, not your ghost.

INT. TRAINING ROOM - DAY

Shoulder iced. Replay of nationals — Nina fourth by a hundredth.
NINA
That's math, not mythology.

INT. LOCKER ROOM - DAY

Teammates celebrate invites. Nina stares at her lane assignment.

INT. COACH'S OFFICE - DAY

Alma slides the invitational invite — last eligible meet.
ALMA
Swim or retire wondering.

INT. DORM ROOM - NIGHT

Nina's father calls. She doesn't pick up. Medal in a drawer, face down.

INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - NIGHT

Solo session. Split fails at 150. Nina hits the lane rope.
NINA
Not clean. Not ever.

EXT. POOL DECK - MORNING

Alma finds Nina stretching in the cold — two hours before warm-ups.
ALMA
Fourth isn't a sentence. It's a split you already survived.

INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - DAY

Blocks. Crowd noise muffled. Nina's world narrows to water.
NINA
(to herself)
Not fourth. Not almost.

INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - DAY

Turn at 150 — elbows high, exactly as coached. Nina drives for the wall. Alma doesn't look at the board yet. She watches Nina's face break open.
ALMA
There she is. That's the split.

FADE OUT.


THE END
